1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:06,217
Traditionally, scientists use a mathematical trick called

2
00:00:06,317 --> 00:00:11,064
'spherical-spline interpolation' to guess missing brainwaves. It

3
00:00:11,164 --> 00:00:14,700
simply averages the signals from nearby sensors.

4
00:00:14,833 --> 00:00:17,594
If you only lose one or two sensors in

5
00:00:17,694 --> 00:00:21,208
a dense cluster, this geometric web works great.

6
00:00:21,333 --> 00:00:24,455
But if you lose most of your sensors, the gaps

7
00:00:24,555 --> 00:00:27,958
are too wide, and the math completely breaks down.

8
00:00:29,433 --> 00:00:34,715
This is where ZUNA's training pays off. Researchers tested ZUNA by

9
00:00:34,815 --> 00:00:39,608
intentionally deleting up to 90 percent of the EEG channels.

10
00:00:39,733 --> 00:00:41,896
As the data gets sparser, the

11
00:00:41,996 --> 00:00:46,033
traditional geometric method's error rate skyrockets.

12
00:00:46,133 --> 00:00:50,184
But ZUNA, relying on the deep patterns it learned from

13
00:00:50,284 --> 00:00:56,795
millions of hours of brainwaves, consistently outputs highly accurate reconstructions.

14
00:00:56,895 --> 00:01:00,408
The wider the gap, the bigger ZUNA's advantage.

15
00:01:01,533 --> 00:01:04,814
What does this mean for the future? Because ZUNA

16
00:01:04,914 --> 00:01:08,970
doesn't just fix broken channels, it can 'imagine' channels

17
00:01:09,070 --> 00:01:12,633
that were never there. We call this superresolution.

18
00:01:12,800 --> 00:01:16,830
By upsampling the data from cheap, comfortable, everyday

19
00:01:16,930 --> 00:01:20,960
consumer headsets, ZUNA could give researchers access to

20
00:01:21,060 --> 00:01:24,500
clinical-grade brain maps anywhere in the world.

21
00:01:25,600 --> 00:01:29,922
While generative AI like ZUNA offers incredible advantages

22
00:01:30,022 --> 00:01:34,497
in handling massive dropout and enabling superresolution, we

23
00:01:34,597 --> 00:01:38,386
must remember the data layer caveats. These imputed

24
00:01:38,486 --> 00:01:43,418
channels are highly realistic estimates, not absolute ground-truth

25
00:01:43,518 --> 00:01:46,850
measurements for critical clinical diagnoses.

